MIOpen (pinned tag rocm-6.4.4): fix ReduceCalculation's Prod (multiply)
kernel to seed its accumulator with the multiplicative identity (1)
instead of the additive identity (0).

WHY
---
src/kernels/MIOpenReduceCalculation.cpp implements both SumForward and
ProdForward (miopenReduceCalculationForward with
MIOPEN_REDUCE_CALCULATION_SUM / _PROD) via one shared kernel template,
parameterized by op. Both variants of the reduction loop
(calculationfwdcontiguous and its parallel-split counterpart,
calculationparallelfwdcontiguous) unconditionally start from:

    FLOAT_ACCUM calculation = static_cast<FLOAT_ACCUM>(0);

then repeatedly apply reduce_func<T, op>::calculate(calculation, val),
which for Sum does `a += b` (correct, 0 is the additive identity) and
for Prod does `a *= b`. Starting Prod's accumulator at 0 means the very
first multiply already yields 0, and every subsequent multiply keeps it
at 0 -- so ProdForward returns an all-zero output for any non-empty
reduction, regardless of the input values.

Confirmed via a standalone MIOpen-only repro (no ORT/model involved):
miopenReduceCalculationForward with MIOPEN_REDUCE_CALCULATION_SUM over a
3D tensor (contiguous, reducing a non-last axis, matching
IsValidLength/IsNotLastDim) returns the correct sum (cos(host_ref,
gpu)=1.0000) across several shapes; the identical harness with
MIOPEN_REDUCE_CALCULATION_PROD instead of SUM returns all zeros
(cos=0.0000) for every shape tested, including a trivial single-element
reduction (a "reduction" over one element should just return that
element unchanged -- it returns 0 instead). Checked upstream: the
identical unfixed code (same accumulator init, same reduce_func) is
still present verbatim as of the newest available MIOpen tag,
rocm-7.2.4 -- this is not something already fixed post-6.4.4.

Likely why it went uncaught despite being this blatant: the whole
ReduceCalculation entry point is gated behind MIOPEN_BETA_API. That
macro is unconditionally defined for every MIOpen build (see
CMakeLists.txt: `add_definitions("-DMIOPEN_BETA_API=1")`), so the
broken code ships in every release, including 6.4.4 and 7.2.4 -- but
"beta" here means the API is new (2023-2024) and Sum is the entry
point real callers actually reach (e.g. ONNX ReduceSum lowering); Prod
looks like a much rarer callsite that few if any inference stacks
(ONNX Runtime's ROCM EP / MIGraphX included) route through this
specific MIOpen function for, so an all-zero-output bug this obvious
could survive unexercised in practice.

This is a plain logic bug in shared, architecture-generic kernel source
(src/kernels/MIOpenReduceCalculation.cpp) with no device-name gating at
all -- it reproduces identically on every ROCm architecture MIOpen
supports, not just gfx803. It's included in this repo's patch set
because we build MIOpen from source here anyway and ship it in the same
image; it is also a legitimate candidate to report upstream to AMD.

WHAT
----
Seed the accumulator with the correct identity element for the
selected op at compile time (op is already a template parameter, so
this resolves via `if constexpr` with no runtime cost): 1 for Prod, 0
for Sum. Applied to both the single-pass and parallel-split reduction
kernels since both duplicate the same accumulator-init line.

Applies to: MIOpen @ rocm-6.4.4, all architectures -- this is not
gated to gfx803 in any way; see reduce-prod-wrong-identity.sh for how
this patch is applied and verified at build time.

diff --git a/src/kernels/MIOpenReduceCalculation.cpp b/src/kernels/MIOpenReduceCalculation.cpp
index d21ae3d..c1105cc 100644
--- a/src/kernels/MIOpenReduceCalculation.cpp
+++ b/src/kernels/MIOpenReduceCalculation.cpp
@@ -53,7 +53,12 @@ __device__ void calculationparallelfwdcontiguous(const TI* __restrict__ x,

     uint64_t parallel_id = slice_local_id / inner_size;

-    FLOAT_ACCUM calculation = static_cast<FLOAT_ACCUM>(0);
+    // REDUCE_PROD_WRONG_IDENTITY_PATCH: seed with this op's identity element,
+    // not unconditionally 0 -- 0 is wrong for Prod (a *= b starting from 0
+    // stays 0 forever) and was making ProdForward always return all zeros.
+    // See reduce-prod-wrong-identity.patch.
+    FLOAT_ACCUM calculation =
+        static_cast<FLOAT_ACCUM>(op == ReduceCalculationOp_t::Prod ? 1 : 0);
     for(uint64_t k = parallel_id; k < reduce_size; k += parallelism_size)
     {
         FLOAT_ACCUM val = CVT_FLOAT2ACCUM(x[input_idx]);
@@ -95,7 +100,9 @@ __device__ void calculationfwdcontiguous(const TI* __restrict__ x,

     uint64_t input_idx = (gid / inner_size) * inner_size * reduce_size + gid % inner_size;

-    FLOAT_ACCUM calculation = static_cast<FLOAT_ACCUM>(0);
+    // REDUCE_PROD_WRONG_IDENTITY_PATCH: see above.
+    FLOAT_ACCUM calculation =
+        static_cast<FLOAT_ACCUM>(op == ReduceCalculationOp_t::Prod ? 1 : 0);
     for(uint64_t k = 0; k < reduce_size; ++k)
     {
         FLOAT_ACCUM val = CVT_FLOAT2ACCUM(x[input_idx]);
